From: echo-penguin
Subject: [PATCH] mtkfb: store all 16 pseudo palette entries at 32 bpp

mtkfb_setcolreg() computed its limit as 1 << bits_per_pixel. At 32 bpp that shift is undefined
and gives 1 on arm64, so every palette entry but 0 was refused and the framebuffer console
drew its text in color 0: black on black. Limit the entries to the 16 the pseudo palette holds.
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt8163/videox/mtkfb.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt8163/videox/mtkfb.c
index 0b8f880d656..94f8d61c623 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt8163/videox/mtkfb.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt8163/videox/mtkfb.c
@@ -259,8 +259,13 @@ static int mtkfb_setcolreg(u_int regno, u_int red, u_int green, u_int blue,
 	MSG_FUNC_ENTER();
 
 	bpp = info->var.bits_per_pixel;
-	m = 1 << bpp;
-	if (regno >= m) {
+	/*
+	 * 1 << 32 is undefined in C, and on arm64 it gives 1: at 32 bpp every entry but 0 was
+	 * refused, so the framebuffer console drew its text black on black. The pseudo palette
+	 * the console uses has 16 entries.
+	 */
+	m = bpp < 32 ? 1U << bpp : 16;
+	if (regno >= m || regno >= 16) {
 		r = -EINVAL;
 		goto exit;
 	}
